.TH FM 1 "2024-05-31" "cfm 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
f \- contextual file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B f
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.RB [ PATH ]
.br
.B f
.RB [ COMMAND ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfm
is a directory listing with instant context. It shows file listing (like ls/exa/lsd) along with git status, build status, TODO count, languages breakdown, and more.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Sorting
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " FIELD"
Sort by field: name, size, date, type, git, extension, version
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timesort
Sort by time modified
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sizesort
Sort by size
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-extensionsort
Sort by file extension
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-gitsort
Sort by git status
.TP
.B \-\-versionsort
Natural sort (version numbers)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sort
No sort, directory order
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order
.TP
.BI \-\-group\-dirs " MODE"
Group directories: none, first, last
.SS Display
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-hidden
Show hidden files (dotfiles)
.TP
.BI \-\-tree " [DEPTH]"
Tree view (0 = unlimited depth)
.TP
.B \-\-group
Group by type (dirs, files, symlinks)
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " PATTERN"
Filter by name pattern
.TP
.BI \-\-max " N"
Limit items displayed
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Less info
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
More info
.SS Output
.TP
.B \-\-json
JSON output
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Plain text output
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B f
Directory listing + context (default)
.TP
.B f PATH
Listing for specific directory
.TP
.B f env
Output shell aliases for current project type
.TP
.B f config
Open configuration file in editor
.TP
.B f daemon stop
Stop the background daemon
.TP
.B f daemon status
Show daemon status
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration file: ~/.config/cfm/config.toml
.PP
Open with: f config
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
[display]
.br
permission = "rwx"
.br
size = "default"
.br
date = "date"
.br
classify = true
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CFM_NO_TODOS
Set to 1 to disable TODO scanning
.TP
.B CFM_NO_PORTS
Set to 1 to disable port detection
.TP
.B CFM_NO_DOCKER
Set to 1 to disable Docker detection
.TP
.B CFM_NO_METRICS
Set to 1 to disable code metrics
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colors (per spec)
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor for f config (default: vi)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Directory listing:
.PP
.RS
f
.RE
.PP
Sort by size:
.PP
.RS
f -S
.RE
.PP
Show dotfiles:
.PP
.RS
f -a
.RE
.PP
Tree view:
.PP
.RS
f --tree
.RE
.PP
JSON output:
.PP
.RS
f --json
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR exa (1),
.BR lsd (1)
